Tom: Yes. My music exam is next week, and I still can''t play one part well.
Mia: Don''t give up. Remember how badly you played a month ago?
Tom: That''s true. I have improved a lot, but it''s so slow.
Mia: Success rarely happens overnight. Just keep practising a little every day.
Tom: You''re right. I decided to practise one hour each evening until the exam.
Mia: That''s the spirit. I''m sure all your hard work will pay off.
Tom: Thanks, Mia. I won''t stop trying until I get it right.', '米娅看出汤姆又在练钢琴而疲惫;汤姆下周有音乐考试,有一段还弹不好;米娅劝他别放弃,想想一个月前弹得多差;汤姆承认进步很大但很慢;米娅说成功很少一蹴而就,每天坚持练一点;汤姆决定每晚练一小时直到考试;米娅鼓励他,努力终会有回报。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Tom look tired?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He has been practising the piano.","He stayed up watching films.","He ran a long race.","He has been ill all week."]},{"q":"When is Tom''s music exam?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Next month.","Next week.","Tomorrow.","Yesterday."]},{"q":"What does Mia say about success?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It rarely happens overnight.","It is impossible for Tom.","It comes only with luck.","It needs no practice."]},{"q":"What does Tom decide to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Give up the exam.","Practise one hour each evening.","Practise only at weekends.","Ask Mia to play for him."]},{"q":"How does Mia feel about Tom''s effort?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She thinks it is a waste of time.","She wants him to stop.","She is sure it will pay off.","She is angry with him."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U2', 'fltrp');
In fact, success rarely happens overnight.
A lot of well-known authors faced rejection again and again.
What made them different was that they refused to give up.
So keep trying, and one day your hard work may finally pay off.', '许多人以为著名作家是一举成名;事实上成功很少一蹴而就;不少知名作家曾一次次遭拒;他们与众不同之处在于不肯放弃;所以请坚持下去,有一天你的努力终会有回报。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many people wrongly believe about writers?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That they never wrote at all.","That they hated reading.","That they were always poor.","That they became successful at once."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say about success?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It rarely happens overnight.","It is easy for everyone.","It never comes to writers.","It depends only on luck."]},{"q":"What did many well-known authors face?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["No problems at all.","Rejection again and again.","Easy and quick fame.","A lack of ideas."]},{"q":"What made these authors different?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They had rich families.","They wrote very fast.","They refused to give up.","They knew famous people."]},{"q":"What advice does the speaker give at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop writing immediately.","Wait for good luck.","Copy other authors.","Keep trying until it pays off."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Dawei: I ran for Head of the Student Committee, but I wasn''t elected.
Jack: I''m sorry to hear that. I''m sure you did your best.
Dawei: I did, but it still hurts. Maybe I''m just not good enough.
Jack: Don''t say that. You should be proud of how hard you worked.
Dawei: Thanks. I suppose one election can''t decide everything.
Jack: Exactly. Try to look on the bright side and cheer up.
Dawei: You''re a good friend, Jack. I already feel a little better.', '杰克看出大伟心烦,问他怎么了;大伟竞选学生会主席却落选;杰克表示遗憾,相信他尽力了;大伟很受伤,觉得自己不够好;杰克让他别这么说,应为努力而自豪;大伟想通一次落选决定不了一切;杰克劝他往好处看、振作起来;大伟感谢这位好友,已经好受了些。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why is Dawei upset?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He was not elected to the committee.","He lost his homework.","He failed a music exam.","He missed the school bus."]},{"q":"What does Jack say about Dawei''s effort?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["That it was useless.","That he is sure Dawei did his best.","That he should have tried harder.","That nobody noticed it."]},{"q":"What does Dawei slowly realise?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["That he will never try again.","That Jack is wrong.","That one election can''t decide everything.","That the result was unfair."]},{"q":"What does Jack advise Dawei to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Forget all his friends.","Stop going to school.","Blame the other students.","Look on the bright side and cheer up."]},{"q":"How does Dawei feel by the end of the talk?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A little better.","Much angrier.","Completely hopeless.","Bored and sleepy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Some of the other boys laughed and told him to quit.
But Ben enjoyed swimming, so he decided to keep practising every day.
Little by little, he grew stronger and faster than before.
Two years later, he won a gold medal at the city games.', '本刚加入游泳队时是最慢的;有些男孩取笑他,叫他退出;但本喜欢游泳,于是决定每天坚持训练;一点点地,他比以前更强更快;两年后,他在市运动会上夺得金牌。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was Ben like when he first joined the team?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He was already the fastest.","He was the slowest of all.","He was the team captain.","He was a famous swimmer."]},{"q":"What did some of the other boys tell him to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To train even harder.","To become the coach.","To quit the team.","To join another sport."]},{"q":"What did Ben decide to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop swimming for good.","Change to a new school.","Laugh at the others.","Keep practising every day."]},{"q":"How did Ben change over time?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He grew stronger and faster.","He grew weaker.","He stayed exactly the same.","He lost interest."]},{"q":"What did Ben win two years later?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A writing prize.","A gold medal at the city games.","A new bike.","A free holiday."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Sam: I''ve already finished my part. I couldn''t wait to start.
Lily: You really are an eager beaver, Sam. That''s a great help.
Sam: Thanks. But I''m worried about Leo. He keeps putting off his part.
Lily: Yes, he''s been dragging his feet all week.
Sam: Maybe we should ask him kindly instead of getting angry.
Lily: Good idea. A wet blanket helps no one; let''s cheer him on.
Sam: Agreed. If we stay positive, he might catch our energy.', '莉莉问小组项目周五截止大家进度如何;萨姆已完成自己的部分,迫不及待就开始了;莉莉夸他是“拼命三郎”,帮了大忙;萨姆担心利奥老是拖着自己那部分;莉莉说他整周都在拖拖拉拉;萨姆建议好言相劝而非发火;莉莉同意,扫兴帮不了人,不如给他打气;萨姆赞同,保持积极也许会感染他。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When is the group project due?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["On Monday.","Next month.","On Friday.","Today."]},{"q":"Why does Lily call Sam an eager beaver?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Because he is often late.","Because he never helps.","Because he is very quiet.","Because he finished his part early."]},{"q":"What is the problem with Leo?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He keeps putting off his part.","He has left the school.","He has done too much.","He is angry with Sam."]},{"q":"What do Sam and Lily decide to do about Leo?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Report him to the teacher.","Ask him kindly and cheer him on.","Do his part for him.","Stop talking to him."]},{"q":"What does Sam hope will happen if they stay positive?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The project will be cancelled.","Leo will leave the group.","Leo might catch their energy.","Lily will do everything."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U2', 'fltrp');
Use your eyes today as if tomorrow you would lose them.
Look closely at the faces of the people you love.
Listen to the mighty music of an orchestra while you still can.
If we treasure each small thing now, every day becomes a blessing.', '一位著名的盲人作家曾给我们一个简单的忠告;今天就用好你的眼睛,仿佛明天就会失去它们;仔细看看你所爱之人的脸;趁还能听,去听管弦乐队雄壮的乐声;若我们珍惜眼前的每件小事,每一天都会成为一种福气。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who gave this piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A young athlete.","A school teacher.","A music student.","A famous blind writer."]},{"q":"How should we use our eyes today?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["As if tomorrow we would lose them.","As if we will never need them.","Only for reading books.","As little as possible."]},{"q":"What should we listen to while we still can?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The noise of traffic.","The mighty music of an orchestra.","Our own voices.","A silent room."]},{"q":"What should we look closely at?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The walls of a museum.","The pages of a book.","The faces of people we love.","Distant mountains."]},{"q":"What happens if we treasure small things now?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["We waste a lot of time.","We grow tired of life.","Nothing changes at all.","Every day becomes a blessing."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U2', 'fltrp');

